    "helpers-long": {
      "source": "# bench: small helper functions called in a hot loop (the shape most library\n# and application code has): clamp, lerp, a mix built from both, and a\n# higher-order helper given a known function\nclamp : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int .\nclamp lo hi x = if x < lo then lo else if x > hi then hi else x.\nlerp : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int .\nlerp a b t = a + (b - a) * t / 256.\nmix : Int -> Int -> Int .\nmix x y = clamp 0 255 (lerp x y 77).\ntwice : (Int -> Int -> Int) -> Int -> Int -> Int .\ntwice f x y = f (f x y) y.\nloop : unsafe Int -> Int -> Int .\nloop n acc = if n == 0 then acc else loop (n - 1) (acc + twice mix (band n 255) (band acc 255)).\nmain = print \"helpers = {loop 100000000 0}\".\n",
      "source_sha256": "6686f260d6aab29eba43c2e6c4d09967f318b5b19143c2d379a6da53c266e7b9",
